void hts_print_backtrace(int fd) {
#ifdef USES_BACKTRACE
  void *stack[256];
  const int size = backtrace(stack, sizeof(stack) / sizeof(stack[0]));
  /* A fault inside the handler lands back here: symbolizing twice interleaves two traces on fd and spends a second budget. */
  static volatile sig_atomic_t entered = 0;
  if (size != 0) {
    backtrace_symbols_fd(stack, size, fd);
    if (symbolize_crash && entered == 0) {
      entered = 1;
      symbolize_backtrace(stack, size, fd);
      entered = 0;
    }
  }
#else
  const char msg[] = "No stack trace available on this OS :(\n";
  if (write(fd, msg, sizeof(msg) - 1) != sizeof(msg) - 1) { /* sorry GCC */ }
#endif
}
The line numbers for the closing lines are approximate. The opening line 214 was confirmed by grep. I trimmed the blank lines and some line breaks from the listing.","Declaration is src/htsbacktrace.h:43. The call site is src/httrack.c:912, as hts_print_backtrace(FD_ERR).","The same file has hts_backtrace_init at about line 207. It sets symbolize_crash from the HTTRACK_NO_SYMBOLIZE environment variable.","configure.ac:70-75 sets DEFAULT_CFLAGS to: -Wall -Wformat -Wformat-security -Wmultichar -Wwrite-strings -Wcast-qual -Wcast-align -Wstrict-prototypes -Wmissing-prototypes -Wmissing-declarations -Wpointer-arith -Wsequence-point -Wnested-externs -D_REENTRANT. configure.ac:76 exports it with AC_SUBST.","configure.ac:82-102 adds more flags to DEFAULT_CFLAGS, each through AX_CHECK_COMPILE_FLAG. They are -Wparentheses, -Winit-self, -Wunused-but-set-parameter, -Waddress, -Wuninitialized, -Wformat=2, -Wformat-nonliteral, -Wmissing-parameter-type, -Wold-style-definition and -Wignored-qualifiers. They also include -Werror=attribute-warning, -Werror=user-defined-warnings, -fstrict-aliasing -Wstrict-aliasing, -fstack-protector-strong (falling back to -fstack-protector), -fstack-clash-protection and -fcf-protection.","configure.ac:111-114 calls AX_ADD_FORTIFY_SOURCE unless CFLAGS contains -fsanitize=. configure.ac:342 adds -fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link to DEFAULT_CFLAGS in the fuzzing case.","Visibility: configure.ac:134-137 runs gl_VISIBILITY, then sets AM_CFLAGS="$AM_CFLAGS $CFLAG_VISIBILITY" and calls AC_SUBST([AM_CFLAGS]). CFLAG_VISIBILITY is -fvisibility=hidden when the compiler supports it. I did not run configure to confirm the value.","configure.ac:124-128 sets CFLAGS_PIE to -fpie. configure.ac:131 adds -Wl,--build-id to the link flags.","src/Makefile.am:18-20 puts @DEFAULT_CFLAGS@ and @THREADS_CFLAGS@ into AM_CPPFLAGS, so the warning and hardening flags are applied through the preprocessor flags, not AM_CFLAGS.","src/Makefile.am:41 sets httrack_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) $(CFLAGS_PIE). Line 42 sets proxytrack_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) $(CFLAGS_PIE) -DNO_MALLOCT -DZLIB_CONST -DHTS_INTHASH_USES_MD5. Line 43 sets htsserver_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) $(CFLAGS_PIE) -DZLIB_CONST -DHTS_INTHASH_USES_MD5.","src/Makefile.am:88 sets libhttrack_la_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) -DLIBHTTRACK_EXPORTS -DZLIB_CONST. Because -fvisibility=hidden comes through AM_CFLAGS, hts_print_backtrace is probably hidden in libhttrack unless it is explicitly exported. I found no visibility attribute in src/htsbacktrace.h, but I only grepped for HTS_PUBLIC and visib.","The top-level Makefile.am has no CFLAGS lines."],"confidence":0.85}

